    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "When your wife tells you that these messages are just normal work communications, what do you think when you hear that? Do you believe her, or do you remain convinced that there's a hidden signal?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "Well, like I was trying to say... I hear her when she says it's just regular office stuff. But no, I don't really believe it. When you watch it happen for a whole year, the timing is just too perfect. It can't be an accident. It's absolutely a private signal, like she's trying to get a message to me that she can't just say to my face. \n\nWhich is strange, because she used to be so direct. Back when we first met, she was actually a high school debate coach. She could argue both sides of literally anything. We went to this one tournament together in Peoria, probably twenty years ago now, and my old Honda Civic's heater completely died on the drive up. It was snowing so hard we couldn't even see the road lines. We had to drive 40 miles an hour the whole way, wearing our heavy winter coats inside the car. I actually had to stop at a gas station to buy extra socks because my toes were going numb. Have you ever bought clothing at a gas station? It’s mostly just hunting gear and those weird neon hats. I think I still have those socks somewhere in the back of my closet, actually. \n\nBut anyway, yeah... I just can't accept that her messages are normal.",
